rr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":83,"oldLines":3,"newStart":83,"newLines":383,"lines":[" *(written by item 10)*"," "," ---","+","+## 1. The baseline ledger and the frozen targets (item 01)","+","+*2026-11-02. Code `learning/obstruction_ledger.py`; tests","+`tests/test_obstruction_ledger.py` (12); files under","+`reports/scratch/obstruction_search/01_ledger/`: `ledger_corpus.csv` (6,376","+rows, every bound on record and `floor0`), `harper12.csv` (the one new","+computation), `ledger_dataset.csv.gz` (16,636 rows), `targets.json`,","+`tables.md` (the tables below, generated), `run.log`, `harper_run.out`,","+`gate_run.out`. Regenerate:","+`nice -n 19 python3 -m learning.obstruction_ledger --stage corpus --workers 8`","+(8 min wall; the Harper run resumes from `harper12.csv`), `--stage dataset","+--workers 8` (6 s), `--stage targets`, `--stage tables`. Size range: corpus","+9–134 customers, all 6,376; dataset classes to 1,024 vertices per component","+(22 classes, all VSPLIB grids, have a larger component and their floors are","+over the rest of the graph); Harper at cap 12 under 60 s per instance.*","+","+### 1.1 What was done","+","+**The record, joined.** For every certified corpus instance: `optimum`,","+`lb_trivial`, `lb_contraction`, `lb_best`, `tw_min_fill`, `ub_best` from","+`learning/data/instances.csv`; `omega`, `contraction`, `exp` (Harper at the","+recorded cap, `exp_cap`), `tw_lo`, `tw_hi`, `tw_exact` from the invariants","+table; Lemma P (`pendant`, optimum units) from loop0010 item 13's","+`reports/scratch/pendant_cliques/harness_values.csv`; the excess","+`e = (n_ones − m) / n`; the collection and the Chu & Stuckey class `(n, m, d)`","+from the file path and the name; the provenance and value of every","+`solutions/` file, read directly (`instances.csv` is a feature table of","+2026-09-25 and lists four 125 × 125 instances as `solution`; the files say","+`certified:refutation` on 6,374 and `certified:bound` on 2, and the values","+agree on all 6,376). The contraction-minor certificates on record were read","+from their files: `reports/scratch/minor_certificates/<name>_m*.json` (claim","+`pw(G) ≥ K`, floor `K + 1`) and","+`reports/scratch/minor_bound/<name>_*_recorded_certificate.json` (`refuted`","+in MOSP units, floor `refuted + 1`; the `.out` files beside them confirm the","+unit: `lower = refuted + 1`). That is **twelve** instances with a file-backed","+minor floor, not the seven the survey's §5 table lists: loop0010's","+`large@recorded` run left certificates for `Random-125-125-2-4_0`, `2-5_0`,","+`4-2_0`, `4-4_0` and `4-5_0` as well. Two values of the survey table have no","+file (`4-1_0` = 54 at 100 vertices min-d, `8-2_0` = 92 at 115–120; logged in","+`reports/scratch/pw_lower_bounds/corpus_minor.out` and `corpus_minor_hi.out`);","+they are carried in the column `minor_survey`, cited, and **not** inside","+`floor0`.","+","+**The one new computation: Harper at cap 12.** `expansion_bound(inst,","+max_t=12, time_budget=60)` on all 6,376 instances, cheapest first, 8 workers","+at `nice -n 19`: 479 s wall, **1.01 core-hours**. 6,341 instances completed","+every level to cap 12; **35 were censored at the 60 s limit** (13 at 76–100","+customers, 22 at 101–134; 33 of them Chu & Stuckey), having completed caps 7","+to 11 — a censored value is still a valid floor, because the module discards","+an abandoned level rather than using its incumbent (its docstring: an","+overestimate of `f(T + 1)` would be a wrong answer, not a slow bound). The","+cap-12 value is never below the recorded `exp` and improves it on **442**","+instances, by up to 21 stacks (`Random-125-125-10-5_0`: 99 = optimum, from","+the recorded cap). Per instance the ledger keeps `harper12`, the cap reached,","+`complete`, seconds and the levels `f(1..t)`.","+","+**`floor0`.** The best floor on record per instance,","+`floor0 = max(lb_best, tw_lo + 1, harper12, lemmaP, minor)`, with the parts","+attaining it in `floor0_source`. The harness's reference is","+`max(lb_best, tw + 1)`; `floor0` adds Harper at cap 12, Lemma P and the minor","+certificates to it.","+","+**The guard.** Every bound column against the optimum, and the dataset's","+cheap floors against the width: **zero violations** on 6,376 × 9 bound","+columns and 16,636 × 4 floors. `tests/test_obstruction_ledger.py` asserts","+this on the committed files.","+","+**The dataset.** For the 16,636 certified classes of","+`paper1/data/dataset/pathwidth_dataset.jsonl.gz`: degeneracy, MMD+ with both","+rules (least-c, min-d) and the largest clique `networkx.find_cliques` reaches","+within 2 s or 200,000 cliques, each per connected component on bit masks, the","+row's value the maximum over its components of at most 1,024 vertices; 48","+core-seconds in all. No row of the jsonl lacks its edge list (the \"78","+header-only graphs\" of the item's brief are not in this file; three classes","+are edgeless, width 0, and are kept); 5 of the 430 `certified:minor` rows","+carry no `minor_certificate` (`pwc-05116`, `05456`, `05480`, `14181`,","+`14639`); 17 clique enumerations were censored.","+","+### 1.2 Findings","+","+1. **On the record, 89.9% of the corpus is closed by a bound** (`floor0`","+   tight on 5,732 of 6,376) against 77.0% for the solver's own `lb_best`","+   (4,909); the instances at gap ≥ 2 fall from 338 to **122**, the mean gap","+   from 0.43 to 0.18 stacks, the maximum from 30 to 23. Treewidth + 1 is the","+   strongest single bound (tight on 5,653; attains `floor0` alone on 898 and","+   is the only part above `lb_best` on 789 tight instances). Harper at cap","+   12 is tight on 4,065, above `lb_best` on 145, and the sole attainer on","+   88. Lemma P is the sole attainer on 5 instances (gap 0 on 2 of them). The","+   minor certificates attain alone on 11 and close 7.","+","+2. **Of the 338, the record already closes 81 (24.0%)**: 67 by exact","+   treewidth alone (the \"67 gap instances would become bound-certified\" of","+   `ml_nature.md` §24, reproduced), **7 by Harper at cap 12 alone**","+   (`Random-100-100-8-2_0`, `Random-125-125-10-3_0`, `Random-125-125-10-5_0`,","+   `Random-75-75-6-3_0`, two Warwick 30-customer instances, `p4040n4_0`),","+   **7 by a minor certificate alone** (`2-1_0`, `2-3_0`, `2-4_0`, `2-5_0`,","+   `4-5_0`, `6-1_0`, `SP4`), none by Lemma P (it beats `lb_best` on 3 by one","+   stack, as `excess_phase_diagram.md` §16 says). Against the harness's","+   reference `max(lb_best, tw + 1)`, which closes 67, `floor0` is strictly","+   above the reference on 104 corpus instances (96 of them in the 338) and","+   closes 14 more. What is left on the 338: 135 at gap 1, 122 at gap ≥ 2","+   (50 at 2, 12 at 3, 9 at 4, 8 at 5, 10 at 6, 33 at 7–23). The survey's \"4","+   of the 125s by minors\" is 7 of 12 on file once loop0010's `large` records","+   are counted (`2-2_0` at 24 of 25, `4-1_0` at 53 of 57, `4-2_0` at 55 of","+   57, `4-4_0` at 50 of 51, `8-2_0` at 87 of 93 are the five short ones; the","+   survey's file-less 54 and 92 would raise two of them by one and five).","+","+3. **Where the record misses is where the solver is slow.** By size band","+   (table a3) the mean `floor0` gap is 0.05 at 9–20 customers, 0.96 at","+   41–60, 5.48 at 76–100 and 4.89 at 101–134; by collection (a2), Chu &","+   Stuckey has 72 instances at gap ≥ 2 out of 200, Faggioli–Bentivoglio 33","+   of 300, and every other collection at most 7. By Chu & Stuckey class (a6):","+   mean `floor0` gap 0.2, 0.2, 0.64, 2.72, 6.64 and 4.96 at 30, 40, 50, 75,","+   100 and 125 customers against `lb_best`'s 0.56, 0.84, 1.40, 4.52, 10.34,","+   14.0; the 125 row sits below the 100 row only because the 125s have minor","+   certificates on record and the 100s have none. Harper at cap 12 is the","+   part that does the work on the **dense** classes (`125-125-10`: mean gap","+   0.2; `100-100-8`: 0.8; `100-50-10`: 4.0 from `lb_best`'s 11.4) and is","+   worse than `lb_best` on the sparse ones (`100-100-2`: 12.2 against 7.8;","+   `75-75-2`: 6.4 against 4.8; `125-125-2`: 15.8 against 9.8) — the ridge","+   classes, where contraction minors are the only part that reaches the","+   optimum (`125-125-2`: 4 of 5 closed, mean gap 0.2). Pathwidth provably","+   exceeds treewidth (`optimum > tw_hi + 1`) on 564 corpus instances and on","+   156 of the 338: on those, no treewidth-side bound can close the gap.","+","+4. **The dataset's cheap floors are tight on 31.4%** (5,231 of 16,636;","+   table b1); MMD+ least-c is the best of the three (tight on 5,059; above","+   min-d on 3,786 classes, below on 552; degeneracy alone 2,130; `ω − 1`","+   970), with gap ≥ 2 on 5,541 classes and a maximum gap of 86 (the","+   Carvalho & Soma MOSP classes, mean gap 63.9, where the floor is a degree","+   bound on a graph of width 133). By provenance: the 3,535","+   `certified:bound` classes are all tight (by construction), 1,696 of the","+   12,630 `certified:refutation` classes, **0 of the 430 `certified:minor`**","+   (mean gap 4.6: a class gets a minor certificate exactly where the cheap","+   floor failed) and 0 of the 41 grids (gap 31.7). The 425 minor","+   certificates all refute `width − 1` (so each proves its class exactly);","+   their minors have median `size / n` 0.505 (0.33–0.84); the rule is min-d","+   on 379 and least-c on 46. Rome (11,199 classes) has mean gap 1.29 and","+   maximum 6; the control-flow graphs 0.41.","+","+5. **The targets, frozen** (`targets.json`, seed 0, ledger sha256","+   `e5918a4c…`): `gap338` 338 (102 of them Chu & Stuckey, 17 at `n ≤ 22`),","+   `cs200` 200, `open24` 24 — every one with a recorded floor (`lower`) from","+   `reports/scratch/dataset_open/results_quick.csv` and","+   `results_quick_rescued.csv`, not from `results.csv` as the plan's §0.3","+   says (that file holds solved classes only): floors are width − 1 on 18","+   classes, width − 2 on `pwc-17043`'s neighbour `pwc-16471`… precisely:","+   `pwc-15933` 4 of 5, `pwc-16471` 6 of 7, `pwc-17043` 2 of 8, `pwc-04526`","+   3 of 10, `pwc-04517` 2 of 10, `pwc-17317` 3 of 10, the other 18 at","+   width − 1 — `rest500` 500 drawn from the 5,940 other corpus instances in","+   proportion to the seven size bands (345 / 140 / 11 / 3 / 0 / 1 / 0; the","+   pool has no instance above 100 customers outside `gap338 ∪ cs200`),","+   disjoint from both, and `small` 4,123 (every corpus instance at","+   `n ≤ 22`). The test re-derives `rest500` from the ledger and the seed.","+","+### 1.3 Kill verdict and what this does not claim","+","+**Kill: none for the item; the guard passed** (no bound on record above a","+certified optimum; no dataset floor above a certified width). The item does","+not claim anything about what a search would find; that `floor0` is the best","+bound obtainable from the record (the minor certificates on file are those","+of twelve instances; Harper is at cap 12 and censored on 35); that the","+dataset's floors are more than the three cheap ones (its 430 minor","+certificates are a fourth, exact by construction, not folded into","+`floor_cheap`); or that the 24 open classes' recorded floors are the best","+the record holds (they are the `lower` of the last quick run).","+","+### 1.4 Tables (generated; `tables.md`)","+","+","+#### (a1) every bound on record, corpus, optimum units","+","+| bound          |   instances |   tight |   gap 1 |   gap ≥ 2 |   mean gap |   max gap |   above optimum |","+|:---------------|------------:|--------:|--------:|----------:|-----------:|----------:|----------------:|","+| lb_trivial     |        6376 |     238 |     726 |      5412 |       6.15 |        86 |               0 |","+| lb_contraction |        6376 |    4164 |    1083 |      1129 |       0.98 |        44 |               0 |","+| lb_best        |        6376 |    4909 |    1129 |       338 |       0.43 |        30 |               0 